```

And `Charset1_2::get_glyph`:
```cpp
inline hb_codepoint_t get_glyph (hb_codepoint_t sid) const
{
  if (sid == 0) return 0;
  hb_codepoint_t glyph = 1;
  for (unsigned int i = 0;; i++)  // UNBOUNDED LOOP!
  {
    if ((ranges[i].first <= sid) && sid <= ranges[i].first + ranges[i].nLeft)
      return glyph + (sid - ranges[i].first);
    glyph += (ranges[i].nLeft + 1);
  }
  return 0;
}
```

So for the OOB read, I need:
1. charset != &Null(Charset) (i.e., CharsetOffset > ExpertSubsetCharset = 2)
2. charset->format == 1 (format 1 charset)
3. The SID from `lookup_standard_encoding_for_sid(code)` is NOT in any of the charset ranges
4. The charset has at least one range (so ranges[0] exists but ranges[1] doesn't)

For step 3: if code=65 ('A'), then `standard_encoding_to_sid[65] = 33`.
If the charset has a range `first=1, nLeft=0` (only SID 1 for glyph 1):
- ranges[0].first=1, ranges[0].nLeft=0
- Loop iteration:1 ≤ 33 but 33 > 1+0=1, so not found in ranges[0]
